# ab-emu-34 — x86_64 Android 14 (API 34) emulator rig.
#
# This is the "modern Android" tier: same W^X and install-policy regime the Galaxy A56's
# Android 16 enforces. It produced PROOF_8 (level win on API 34) and PROOF_9 (advance into
# level 2), and it is the rig that caught the missing `-lm` link bug — which would have
# crashed the shim on launch on the A56 with `UnsatisfiedLinkError: cannot locate symbol
# "sin"`. API 25 masked that; modern bionic does not. Do not retire this tier.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROVENANCE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The original ab-emu-34:latest was NOT built from a Dockerfile. It was produced
# imperatively: a container was started from ab-emu:latest, a setup script was run inside
# it, and the result was `docker commit`ed. A committed image has no build recipe, so the
# recipe below was recovered from the image's own recorded config
# (`docker inspect ab-emu-34:latest --format '{{json .Config.Cmd}}'`), which preserved the
# exact setup command verbatim. The RUN steps below are that command, split into layers.
#
# `FROM ab-emu:latest` is not a convenience — it is what actually happened, and the
# resulting image state was verified to match:
#
#   ab-emu:latest     AVDs: abtest                    system-images: android-25
#   ab-emu-34:latest  AVDs: abtest, abtest34          system-images: android-25, android-34
#
# So ab-emu-34 is a strict superset and can run the API 25 scripts too. Build ab-emu first:
#
#   docker build -f port/docker/Dockerfile.ab-emu    -t ab-emu    port/docker
#   docker build -f port/docker/Dockerfile.ab-emu-34 -t ab-emu-34 port/docker
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NETWORK POLICY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Building this image requires network (sdkmanager fetches the android-34 system image).
# Every RUN of the image is launched `--network none`. See the same section in
# Dockerfile.ab-emu, and port/validation/README.md, for the full rationale.
# Treat the build host as internet-reachable: never `-p`/`--publish`, never `--network host`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPRODUCIBILITY LIMITATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inherits every float described in Dockerfile.ab-emu, plus one of its own: Google revises
# system images in place, so `system-images;android-34;default;x86_64` is not a fixed
# artifact. Version installed in the image that generated the committed evidence:
#
#   system-images;android-34;default;x86_64     Pkg.Revision = 2
#
# The inherited /IMAGE_VERSIONS is extended with the android-34 entry below.

# BASE is overridable so this image can be rebuilt and diffed against the existing
# ab-emu-34:latest without overwriting the working ab-emu:latest that the committed
# evidence was generated on:  --build-arg BASE=ab-emu:verify
ARG BASE=ab-emu:latest
FROM ${BASE}

RUN yes | sdkmanager "system-images;android-34;default;x86_64" >/tmp/sdk.log 2>&1

RUN echo "no" | avdmanager create avd -n abtest34 \
        -k "system-images;android-34;default;x86_64" --force >/tmp/avd.log 2>&1

# --- ADDITION: the original recipe printed AVD_OK/AVD_FAIL and carried on regardless.
# --- Fail the build instead, so a broken image can never be published as a working one.
RUN set -e; \
    test -f "$HOME/.android/avd/abtest34.avd/config.ini" || { echo "FATAL: AVD abtest34 was not created"; cat /tmp/avd.log; exit 1; }; \
    test -f "$HOME/.android/avd/abtest.avd/config.ini"   || { echo "FATAL: inherited AVD abtest is missing"; exit 1; }; \
    { echo -n "sysimg-34      "; grep Pkg.Revision $ANDROID_SDK_ROOT/system-images/android-34/default/x86_64/source.properties; } >> /IMAGE_VERSIONS; \
    cat /IMAGE_VERSIONS

CMD ["/bin/bash"]
